  "content": {
    "id": "p14-q6-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "6",
    "prompt": "We can find the area of quadrilaterals by dividing them into two triangular parts.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p14-q6-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Each side of a rhombus is $30\\text{ m}$ and its longer diagonal is $48\\text{ m}$. Find the area of the rhombus.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$864\\text{ m}^2$.\n\nDivide along the diagonal, use Heron’s formula and double the triangle’s area.",
          "worked": "The diagonal divides the rhombus into two congruent triangles with sides $30$, $30$ and $48$ metres.\n$$\\begin{align*}s&=\\frac{30+30+48}{2}=54\\\\A_{\\text{triangle}}&=\\sqrt{54(54-30)(54-30)(54-48)}\\\\A_{\\text{triangle}}&=\\sqrt{54\\times24\\times24\\times6}\\\\A_{\\text{triangle}}&=432\\text{ m}^2\\\\A_{\\text{rhombus}}&=2\\times432\\\\A_{\\text{rhombus}}&=864\\text{ m}^2\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 68
      },
      {
        "id": "p14-q6-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "A rhombus has a perimeter of $100\\text{ cm}$ and one of its diagonals is $40\\text{ cm}$. Find the area of the rhombus.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$600\\text{ cm}^2$.\n\nEach side is $25\\text{ cm}$; apply Heron’s formula to one triangular half and double its area.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Side length}&=\\frac{100}{4}=25\\text{ cm}\\end{align*}$$\nThe diagonal divides the rhombus into two congruent triangles with sides $25$, $25$ and $40$ centimetres.\n$$\\begin{align*}s&=\\frac{25+25+40}{2}=45\\\\A_{\\text{triangle}}&=\\sqrt{45(45-25)(45-25)(45-40)}\\\\A_{\\text{triangle}}&=\\sqrt{45\\times20\\times20\\times5}\\\\A_{\\text{triangle}}&=300\\text{ cm}^2\\\\A_{\\text{rhombus}}&=2\\times300\\\\A_{\\text{rhombus}}&=600\\text{ cm}^2\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 78
      }
    ]
  },
